    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0356" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13673½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-06T03:00:00-04:00">August 6, 1941—3
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2984. Personal for the Ambassador. Following is the President’s reply to your No.
                    3428, August 5, 10 p.m.: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Think highly inadvisable make any statement at this time. In my
                            judgement all that need be said is that Prime Minister is on short
                            vacation. References to accompanying officers especially bad. Any
                            statement <pb facs="0357" n="345" xml:id="pg345"/> now is direct
                            invitation to Germans to attack him and his party going and returning.
                            When in doubt say nothing. Roosevelt.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
